.superpowers/
/build/*
!build/appicon.png
# The icon illustration is a BUILD INPUT, not a build output: tools/genicon
# reads it to produce the iconset, so it has to be committed.
!build/icon-artwork.png
!build/darwin/
/bin
/dr-markdown
/dr-markdown.exe
*.app
.DS_Store
/frontend/dist/wailsjs/

# Architext generated static builds.
docs/architext/dist/
docs/architext/.architext-write.lock/

# Claude Code local scaffolding: personal workflow state, never shared.
.claude/

# architext doctor writes a timestamped backup beside any file it repairs. It is
# working state to reconcile and delete, never a repository artifact — and it is
# exactly the kind of file `git add -A` sweeps in unnoticed. One already reached
# a commit that way.
docs/architext/data/**/*.bak

# `go build ./tools/<x>` drops the compiled binary in the repo root under the
# package name. They are build output, not source — one reached a commit.
/genicon
/genbanner
/genbound
/dr-markdown

# Ephemeral workflow documentation is NEVER committed. Plans, specs, scratch
# analysis, session notes, skill scaffolding — by-products of how the work was
# done, not artefacts the project needs.
#
# `.superpowers/` was ignored; `docs/superpowers/` was not, so 38 files and 384K
# were tracked on main and shipped in every release for weeks, and were cited 33
# times from decision and release records before anyone noticed.
#
# Durable reasoning goes in a normal location — docs/decisions, docs/releases,
# the README — not behind a link to a file that should not be in the repository.
docs/superpowers/
.claude/skills/**/output/
**/scratchpad/
